      "tree_id": "8661ca3f0f4ac1ef25cf788e815775f70abc8b23",
      "message": "A sharded CI build notifies once, when its check suite finishes\n\nA passing or cancelled check_run no longer wakes a PR subscriber. The\ncheck_suite `completed` delivery reports the result once every run in the\nsuite has finished, pass or fail. A failed, timed-out or action-required\ncheck_run still wakes the subscriber the moment it arrives.\n\ncheck_suite goes through the same superseded-commit check and the same\nneutral/skipped/stale drop as check_run, now shared in `_ci_topics`.\n\nThe two check_suite fixtures are real deliveries from labkit (#514,\nsuccess, 9 runs) and agent-bus (push to main, skipped, no PR).\n\nThe webhook setup table in infra/cloud/README.md now lists every event the\nbridge reads, including check_suite; a hook without it gets no notice of a\ngreen build.\n\nCloses #350\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XEC2HFFH318qFYCQ1M9LFK",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-27T00:26:08Z",
      "author": {
        "name": "Dan Barua",
        "email": "danbarua@gmail.com"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Dan Barua",
        "email": "danbarua@gmail.com"
      }
    }
  },
